   "en": "⟦0⟧ only had an army equipped with obsolete weapons and a tiny navy that was composed of two old German gunboats and four Italian torpedo boats. Its quick defeat was no surprise, yet the Italians had some trouble with such a small army. Fascist ⟦1⟧ set up Albania as its protectorate or puppet state. It was practically a union between ⟦2⟧ and Albania, officially led by Italian King Victor Emmanuel III and his government: Albania was led by Italian governors, after being militarily occupied by ⟦3⟧, from 1939 until 1943. During this time, Albania ceased to exist as an independent country and became an autonomous part of the Italian Empire.",
